WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.240
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.150
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.900
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.600
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.700
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.070
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:46.000
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.250
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.520
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.260
What is truly precious?

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:14.920
The Girl from America

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.110
Bakura!

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.480
Everyone.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.400
You're awake, Mokuba.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.410
Thank goodness.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.710
Hey!

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.690
Yugi!

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.720
Where have you been?

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.390
Sorry.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.190
Mokuba, you're free now.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.160
What about my brother?

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.710
Where's my big brother?

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.400
Mokuba.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.450
Croquet.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.670
Pegasus has been taken to a hospital.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.180
Did Bakura do something?

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.890
But we threw away the Millennium Ring.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.050
It must've been someone else.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:23.960
Here.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.490
What's this?

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.190
It's a card called The Ties of Friendship.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.060
Pegasus instructed me to give it to Yugi Muto.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.100
You both dueled masterfully.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.540
This is a check for the prize money.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.080
Jonouchi...

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.400
Congrats, Jonouchi.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.090
Shizuka will now be healed.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.240
Yeah.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.020
Shizuka, just wait for me.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.130
Jonouchi...

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.350
I'll be leaving.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.570
Yugi, if Mokuba is no longer sealed away, that might mean...

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.200
Yeah!

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.770
Grandpa should be free too!

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.460
Yugi...

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:37.660
Big brother!

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.000
Big brother!

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.720
Where could Kaiba have gone?

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.750
Big brother!

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.680
Big brother!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.680
Mokuba.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:07.590
You brothers better take care of each other forever.  Sheesh.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.470
Big brother, I kept our Kaiba Corporation safe.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.110
I see.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:26.480
They never realized that this was the card key to the storage facility containing the important documents.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.760
I'm proud of you, Mokuba.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.750
Good job protecting Kaiba Corporation.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:37.960
Yugi, it seems you helped Mokuba.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.820
I owe you one.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.490
You don't owe me anything.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:47.200
But Yugi, our duel isn't over yet.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:48.730
I know.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:54.020
The day will come when we face each other to decide who is the true winner.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.480
I look forward to that day.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.880
We finally did it.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.890
Thank you.  It's all due to you.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.290
The two of us earned this victory.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.790
No, it wasn't just the two of us.

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:18.620
Yeah.  We all earned this victory together.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:19.770
Yeah.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.950
How are we supposed to get off this island?

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.510
Wait up, Kaiba!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.220
Don't leave me behind!

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.720
I got the Millennium Eye.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:55.770
Grandpa!

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:58.010
Grandpa!

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:59.070
Yugi!

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.020
I'm home, Grandpa.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.880
Well done, Yugi.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.680
I couldn't have done it without everyone.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.650
That's right.  Everyone.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.130
Especially me.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:24.390
Okay, let's celebrate tonight with a delicious meal.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.170
How lucky!

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.400
Excellent!

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.280
Grandpa, the doctor said you should take it easy.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.800
What are you talking about?  I'm fit as a fiddle!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.000
Grandpa?

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.770
Are you okay, Grandpa?

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.760
Ouch!  My back!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.400
Who's that?

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:51.550
Do you know her?

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.560
Are you Sugoroku Muto?

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.560
Yes I am.  And you are?

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.240
My name is Rebecca.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.440
I arrived this morning from America.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.700
Sheesh, you're late!

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.270
How dare you keep a lady waiting!

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:10.600
Lady?

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.380
What?  Are you saying that I'm not a lady?

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:18.780
Hey, why did a little kid like you come all the way to Japan by herself?

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:19.920
Goddamn!

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:22.980
I won't talk to someone so vulgar.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.650
Right, Teddy?

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.500
What did you say?

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.830
Rebecca, why did you come to see me?

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:31.060
Give it back!

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:32.660
Give what back?

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.660
Give back Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:40.470
Give it back now!  It's mine!

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.170
But that card was...

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:54.060
Blue-Eyes White Dragon is a super powerful card that's originally from America.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:59.860
Which means America's strongest duelist should have it, and that person is me!

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:01.590
Right, Teddy?

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.090
America's strongest duelist?

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.700
Yes.  I'm America's champion.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.800
America's champion?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:10.700
That's right.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.110
C'mon now.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:14.300
That's not a good joke.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.960
She's not lying.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.940
I remember seeing a magazine article.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:24.220
A 12 year-old created a sensation by winning the American championship.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.480
She's a dueling prodigy.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:32.140
Hey, this stuck-up brat is the American champion?

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:33.190
You must be kidding.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:34.660
What's your problem?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.240
Are you making fun of the American champion?

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:42.520
Hush up!  I finished second in Duelist Kingdom.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:46.480
Yeah, but you were 8th in the regionals until recently.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.440
Whose side are you on?

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.880
I know about that.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.480
First place in Duelist Kingdom was Yugi Muto.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.240
Second place was Jonouchi Katsuya.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:01.050
But if you're not in first place, it's the same as being in last place.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.760
Right, Teddy?

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.320
How dare you!

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:11.560
Rebecca, Blue-Eyes White Dragon is a very important card for me.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.400
Of course it is.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.600
You traveled all the way to America to steal it.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:20.360
Steal?  Rebecca, you're mistaken.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.470
Grandpa is-

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:24.760
That's what Bandit Keith told me.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.210
He said that Blue-Eyes was stolen.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.620
That idiot!  How dare he say that!

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:37.020
Blue-Eyes belongs to me, the American champion!  Give it back!

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.770
Rebecca, that card is...

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.040
What?

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.690
I see.  You don't want to give it back.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:48.360
Wait a sec!  That's not what I mean.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:51.070
It's just that...  Well...

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:52.700
Then I challenge you!

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.100
Duel!

00:09:56.380 --> 00:10:00.940
Sugoroku Muto, you give Blue-Eyes back to me if I win!  Got it?

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:03.650
Hey, that's enough!

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.230
Got it?

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.550
Arrange for a Duel Ring!

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:08.700
Hurry up!

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.140
Hooray!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.380
Please, Mokuba.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.800
I guess so.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:44.870
The Duel Rings are booked for the next three months.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.990
But I'll make an exception.

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:48.380
Thank you.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.280
Take me there now!

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:53.150
Let's go!  Hurry up!

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.360
This is the Duel Ring?

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.770
Let's begin, Sugoroku Muto.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:02.960
Grandpa!

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:05.200
I'll be fine, Yugi.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.040
But...

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:12.650
Come on!  How long do you plan to keep the American champion waiting?

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.750
Rebecca, I'll take you on!

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.300
Yugi!

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:19.970
Grandpa was just released from the hospital.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.090
He's in no shape to duel.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:24.160
Okay, fine.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:29.780
Yugi Muto, the champion of Duelist Kingdom, is worthy of being my opponent.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:34.700
But I can't imagine how you'll be able to defeat a dueling prodigy like me.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.420
Right, Teddy?

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.700
What's with her super bratty attitude?

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.850
Grandpa, watch from here.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.850
Sorry, Yugi.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.350
I leave it to you.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.060
Duel!

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.030
Are you sure about this?

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:02.220
About what?

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:07.540
I've said this many times, but I'm the American champion because I'm a prodigy.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.100
Right, Teddy?

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:11.140
Yes, Rebecca.

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:13.100
You're a prodigy!  A genius!

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:19.060
What's her true purpose?

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.740
Why does she care so much about Blue-Eyes?

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.660
Witch of the Black Forest in attack position.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:33.420
Come out, my cute monster!

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.800
Witch of the Black Forest.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:48.380
Bandit Keith and Pegasus J. Crawford gave me a pretty good idea about American dueling style.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:50.640
He's so slow, Teddy.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.950
I wish he would take his turn.

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:55.320
I play this!

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.920
I summon Celtic Guardian.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:00.920
Attack!

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:08.700
Witch of the Black Forest is destroyed.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:09.860
No!

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:15.500
My Witch of the Black Forest was sent to the graveyard.  What should I do?

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:18.870
Huh?  What's that?  Oh, I see!

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:22.340
When Witch of the Black Forest is sent to the graveyard...

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:26.930
...I can add a monster with 1500-or-fewer defense points from my deck to my hand.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:29.770
Then I shuffle my deck.

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:33.490
Thank you!  Teddy, you're the best!

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:42.600
Rebecca, it's your turn.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:45.470
I'm thinking, so don't talk to me!

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.470
Hmm, what should I do?

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.470
Is she really the American champion?

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.190
Should I use this?

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.880
Okay, I'll use it!

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.880
Sangan in attack position.

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:05.690
Sangan is so cute!

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:08.690
Rebecca, it's also going to the graveyard.

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:09.460
What?

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:10.700
Battle!

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:19.680
My Sangan went to the graveyard!

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:20.530
Goddamn!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:25.070
C'mon, you knew it was going to lose from the start!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:28.780
Teddy, that boy is bullying me.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.810
I'm not bullying you!

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:33.350
Huh?  What did you say?

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.220
We haven't lost yet?

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:39.450
Use Sangan's effect to draw a monster from my deck?

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:41.820
Okay!

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.180
That girl is weird.

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.770
Aren't all prodigies like that?

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:52.430
That twerp!  I'll never accept that she's a champion!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.970
I've seen this duel before...

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.710
It's my turn.  Here I go!

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.450
Her attitude has suddenly changed.

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:10.970
The spell card Tribute to The Doomed.

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:18.190
By discarding a card from my hand, I can destroy one of your monsters on the field!

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.760
Celtic Guardian is destroyed!

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.970
Then I play a card in defense position.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:41.660
It's only going to get more interesting.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:44.880
I promise to get Blue-Eyes back.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.110
What just happened?

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:49.740
She's like a totally different person.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:52.480
She's only 12, but she's the American champion!

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:53.890
Be careful, Yugi!

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.600
She's a different person than before.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.950
I have to proceed carefully.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:01.630
It's my turn.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:04.360
I attack with Summoned Skull!

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:10.240
You fell for it.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:13.480
I have Millennium Shield!

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:14.980
What?

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:17.120
Battle!

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:24.600
This is an impenetrable defense!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.930
Woohoo!  We did it, Teddy!

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:31.440
She's actually strong!

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:33.580
She's no ordinary girl.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.500
Millennium Shield.  Has a nice ring to it, doesn't it?

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:45.300
Yes.  This is the definition of an impenetrable defense.

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.050
Let's continue.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.920
Yes, Professor Hopkins.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:53.300
Sugoroku, call me Arthur.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.820
This duel is the same as that time.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.660
Aww, why are you so surprised?  That's rude.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.870
I'm a prodigy.  Doing this was a cinch.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:09.270
Teddy, we're getting to the good part.

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:12.770
The spell card Ring of Magnetism.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:19.110
Ring of Magnetism?

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:24.180
If I recall, equipping that card lowers your defense points.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:29.130
Teddy, it looks like he's confused.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:32.170
What a fool.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:35.150
I'll pass this turn.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:37.900
Oh, you want to see how things play out.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:39.370
Then here I go!

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.370
Cannon Soldier in attack position.

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.370
This is bad!

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:55.480
Cannon Soldier can attack a player directly by tributing a monster.

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.180
Don't worry, Grandpa.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:18:01.100
Since Cannon Soldier has fewer attack points, Summoned Skull will destroy it.

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:09.570
Summoned Skull attacks Cannon Soldier!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:16.540
That won't work!  Ring of Magnetism activates!

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:26.450
Ring of Magnetism draws your monster's attack to it!

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:33.440
You're only allowed to attack my Millennium Shield that's equipped with Ring of Magnetism.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:37.020
And you can't easily destroy it because it has 2500 defense points!

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:42.660
Summoned Skull's attack points and Millennium Shield's defense points are equal.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:46.800
But if they're equal, you can't destroy a monster in defense position.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.800
Isn't this fun, Teddy?

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:52.700
It's my turn.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:01.410
I've been waiting for this, but now isn't the time to play it.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:05.600
I summon Witch of the Black Forest in attack position!

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:14.900
I tribute Witch of the Black Forest so that Cannon Soldier can attack you directly!

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.730
There's one more thing.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:36.080
Witch of the Black Forest's effect allows me to draw a card from my deck.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:40.860
I can see why that kid says she's #1 in America.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.490
Is that girl...

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:49.530
I'll show you how much it hurts to have your Blue-Eyes taken from you!

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:51.100
What do you mean?

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:55.600
It is her!  Rebecca, you're...

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:58.170
You finally realized.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.970
Yes, my name is Rebecca Hopkins.

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:09.450
I'm the granddaughter of Arthur Hopkins, and you stole his precious Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:11.160
Say what?

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:15.220
You're my grandpa's best friend's granddaughter?

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.920
That's right.

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:22.600
I'll make you feel every bit of my grandfather's resentment.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.580
Prepare yourself!

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:33.120
That brat is Grandpa's best friend's granddaughter?

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:39.160
Yugi is dueling to clear Grandpa's name, but Rebecca is America's champion.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.960
Her tactics are driving Yugi into a corner.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:48.440
What?  This duel is the same as the one Grandpa had against his friend?

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:50.880
That means the outcome will be...

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:53.720
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Deadly Shadow Ghoul

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:55.420
Duel, standby!

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:07.450
The flask glistens

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:15.300
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:24.270
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:32.050
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:37.880
Shower of happiness

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:41.990
I will shower you with it

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:50.260
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:54.500
Shower of happiness

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:58.630
You are not alone

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:05.350
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
